WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.480
<b>5/26/2000</b>

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.040
Prepare yourselves, BETA.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.640
You won't make it out of Japan alive!

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:41.170
Wh-

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.430
A division-sized group of BETA has 
re-landed all across Miho Bay!

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:48.550
More than 20,000?

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:53.060
They're probably swarming from 
the continent, White Fang 1.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:56.150
Hydra 1? What's your situation?

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.570
We have two companies of Imperial 
Guard, and we're holding!

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.230
But we were counting on help from the 
Imperial Army and they're panicking.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.750
A sneak attack took out the HQ in Yonago.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:13.760
We will spread out and attempt to delay them.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:20.260
We'll buy time for the remaining Imperial 
Forces to retreat and regroup behind us.

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.020
There's more than 20,000 of them.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.250
Even for the Takemikazuchi...

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.240
Both soldiers and equipment are 
critical to the Empire's survival.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.920
We can't lose them.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.270
Kyoko-sama, you...

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.840
What's that look, Yui?

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:44.950
We Imperial Guard are always at 
the front lines of the battle.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.370
And when we retreat, we cover the rear.

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:53.730
If you don't stay there, the forces at 
Izumo will be attacked from two directions,

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.600
and the whole army's supply 
train will be cut off.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:58.710
You know that, right?

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:02.200
I do.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.250
Keep the Empire safe for me.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.450
No.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.750
Please show us the pride of the Imperial 
Guard, and last until reinforcements arrive!

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:12.930
Leave it to me.

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:19.530
Kyoko-sama!

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.440
Let us go as well.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:58.710
11 o' clock. Company sized 
group of around 3000.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:04.480
They're heading to the northwest.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.740
A group of fleeing BETA.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.250
Inferior life forms...

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:09.720
Don't let a single one of them escape!

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.570
All squads, follow me!

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.370
As we originally planned,

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:52.350
we will destroy the Prototype 
Type 99 EM Radiation Cannon here.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:00.040
No way...

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.750
What's going on?

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:05.960
All the BETA are heading for this hangar?

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:30.600
<b>The Price of a Choice</b>

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:40.810
Aim for the core module between the 
grip guard and the coolant unit.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.740
If you can destroy it that will be enough.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:45.340
You're sure about this, right?

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:48.010
Stop asking and focus on the shot.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:49.230
Alright.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:55.430
I promise you. I'll bring your 
precious 94 Second back unharmed.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:57.360
I promise.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.740
And this EM Radiation Cannon too.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:17.800
Well?

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.360
Did you destroy the core module?

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:23.100
No, we have a problem.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.770
Sorry, but I missed.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:28.820
The core module's only half destroyed.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:29.530
What?

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:34.030
The thick frame kept me from 
getting a direct hit on it.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.970
Now what?

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:45.570
I can carry it by hand now. Do you 
still want me to leave it here?

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:49.640
You did that deliberately.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:54.330
At this range, and with your skills, 
it's impossible for you to miss.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:55.560
True.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:58.430
Just think of it as a reward, or something.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:00.680
You worked really hard.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:04.060
Bridges, you...

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:08.490
And would you stop calling 
me by my last name?

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.060
You can call me Yuuya.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:17.930
W-What are you saying all of a sudden?

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:21.910
What? You were just calling me that.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:25.240
H-H-How did you...

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:30.420
I had the external mic on so 
I could see if you were alive.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:33.330
Yuuya...

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:41.580
If you're going to call me that when 
I'm not around, do it all the time.

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.340
And it's okay now?

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:48.600
It took a while, but I've 
finally admitted it.

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:52.510
That you're an amazing Eishi.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.020
We're part of a team 
working for the same goal.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:59.010
For us to call each other by our 
first names is nothing special-

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.050
Argos 1, come in!

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:03.960
What's wrong, Argos 4?

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:09.700
All the BETA are heading for your hangar!

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:18.720
<b>Approximately 50 km behind the D-04 Supply Base</b>

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:21.410
A change in the advancing pattern of the BETA forces!

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:23.220
W-What are they...?

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.050
It's like something is drawing them forward!

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.480
No match in the database.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.750
This is a new pattern.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:33.720
All the BETA are heading for D-04!

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.610
It appears they're heading 
for the hangar block!

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:41.750
I don't believe the Zhar Battalion will be 
able to handle this situation on their own.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:44.610
We should consider sending reinforcements.

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:48.730
And according to the 
information we just received,

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:51.810
one Imperial Army officer 
is still in that hangar.

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:56.370
Two of the XFJ TSFs have gone to rescue her.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:09:04.770
I believe we should send the Idar Flight to 
"rescue" them, and ensure we recover the new cannon.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.510
Lt. Sandek,

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.860
Launch all the bombers on standby.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:15.530
Destroy the BETA and the 
base until nothing is left.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:17.290
Yes.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:20.950
Until there are no traces left.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:25.690
But Commander, that will 
cost us the cannon...

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:30.000
Your plan failed, Comrade Sandek.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:32.750
You need to know when to give up.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:36.750
If you continue to be greedy, 
it will cost you your life.

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:40.860
If I may speak freely, Comrade, the 
sacrifices we've already made...

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:42.380
Comrade Lieutenant.

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:46.630
Do you intend to put my 
own position in danger?

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:49.630
Yes sir.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:56.080
I will order the Zhar Battalion to 
rescue the officer and the XFJ TSFs...

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.860
Comrade Sandek.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:03.860
Your orders were to eliminate all traces.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:07.610
Think about it.

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:09.870
Amidst all this confusion,

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:15.970
both you and I should have no means 
of knowing that they are even there.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.680
Then I'll order the Zhar Battalion to re-

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:21.680
All traces.

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:25.990
We'll need to bring in replacements again.

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:38.390
Damn it!

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:39.350
Is the Core Module okay?

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:42.780
Get off!

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.210
No! Lieutenant!

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:51.180
Without a suit for her, I can't fight any more.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:53.130
She won't last!

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:57.770
Damn it!

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:10.390
Argos 4, we're leaving!

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:15.410
Argos 4, we're leaving!

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:17.690
Get out-

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:20.980
Destroyer Class?

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:29.410
Lieutenant!

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:42.130
What the hell?

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:54.500
A Fort Class?

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:57.100
Its whip knocked me out of the sky?

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:58.800
Retreat.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.150
Lieutenant!

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:03.480
The 94 Second can't fight a Fort right now.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:05.870
Get out of here.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.070
I'd love to, but...

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.730
Fall back, Argos 1!

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:37.030
You saved me.

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:38.680
Get the Lieutenant out of here!

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:40.840
I'll hold them off.

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:41.650
No.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.190
You take the Lieutenant.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:46.700
Prepare to receive her.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:51.020
I'm ashamed to say it 
but this TSF is a wreck.

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:56.200
If I try a long jump I 
could crash at any time.

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:57.290
Wait, Bridges-

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:58.460
Hurry!

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:00.910
It's safer for her on your TSF.

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:04.410
Alright.

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:08.840
Lieutenant, watch your step.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:12.150
Be careful.

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:15.790
You just tried fighting 
a BETA all by yourself.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:21.510
Sorry.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.880
I promised you, remember?

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:29.500
That I'd get your EM 
Radiation Cannon back safe.

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:33.580
In the end I couldn't 
even get the core module.

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:38.750
But I'll make sure the 94 
Second makes it back okay.

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:43.780
Well, I can't get it back unharmed anymore.

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:48.500
So... forgive me, Lt. Takamura.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:51.060
Now let's go.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:55.510
Yui.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:00.650
You need to stop calling me by my last name.

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:01.950
What?

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.830
You can call me Yui.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.650
What did you say? I can't hear you.

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:13.460
Say that again.

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:18.820
If you want me to forgive you, 
bring back the Shiranui 2 okay!

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:19.660
Got it?

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:22.610
Yeah. Roger.

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:44.390
Where are you going, Sergeant?

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:46.880
To the UN Command Base.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.880
I want to know what's going 
on at that supply base.

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:50.940
Lieutenant?

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.420
What's going on there?

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:55.420
I've already looked into it.

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:57.260
Then we can send a rescue?

00:14:59.030 --> 00:14:59.580
Lieutenant?

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:03.690
We don't know if Lt. Takamura 
and the pilots are safe.

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:08.100
And it looks like the Soviets 
have their own plans.

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:10.790
Plans? You mean rescue plans right?

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.000
I don't know.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:16.670
They aren't sharing any information with the 
UN and aren't responding to our requests.

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:20.490
They're keeping the Iron Curtain 
down even after all this?

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:21.760
That's not all.

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:27.180
I've got unconfirmed reports 
of a large number of bombers.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:33.700
We realized it when they said there was 
a no-fly zone 20km around the base.

00:15:34.310 --> 00:15:35.760
Bombers?

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:37.540
And a no-fly zone?

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.710
If they're heading for the base...

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:43.050
No way.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:48.160
This is Grom Leader. {Russian for "Thunder"}

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:50.230
All bombers in flight.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.720
15 minutes until attack run.

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:55.120
Kamchatsky control, roger.

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:57.040
Continue the operation.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:59.550
Repeat. Continue the operation.

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:26.610
The Lieutenant doesn't have a suit, so I 
can't use my rocket motor for the takeoff.

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:29.330
There's so many...

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:33.490
There's not that many on the taxiway.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:37.250
That gives me plenty of room for takeoff.

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:40.650
This is my last chance to get out of here.

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:42.720
Argos 1.

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:45.630
Let's use the taxiway so 
we can save some fuel.

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:48.980
Do a long jump when your 
speed gets high enough.

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.140
We'll jump right over the BETA.

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:52.340
Roger.

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:55.210
Just to say it again: don't worry about me.

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:58.150
And you know what you need to do too, right?

00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:01.660
No fighting, just head for the hills, sure.

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.030
That's right.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:10.750
The coast is clear.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.470
On the count of 5...

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:17.830
5, 4, 3, 2, 1...

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:18.830
Go!

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:29.730
Damn it!

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:33.870
My engine can't generate enough power!

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:38.530
What?

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:39.480
What's wrong?

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:42.500
Argos 1 is falling behind.

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:48.430
The jump unit was more badly 
damaged than we thought.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:50.990
His propulsion isn't where it needs to be.

00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:53.270
At this rate...

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:05.500
If I dodge here I won't have 
enough distance to take off.

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:13.010
Do I have to use the rocket motor?

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:22.400
He's just shooting their 
legs so he can save ammo?

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:24.170
Yuuya...

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:25.920
You're amazing.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:29.620
Did something happen with Lt. Bridges?

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:35.860
Stella!

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:39.500
He's telling me to go?

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:42.340
Yuuya...

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:44.940
You're that certain...

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:46.360
Ensign Bremer.

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:48.110
What's going on?

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:49.020
Where's the Shiranui?

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:53.220
Alright.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:57.520
I'll believe in you, Yuuya!

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.480
We took off?

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:18.150
Yuuya...

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:19.710
What happened to Yuuya?

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:25.210
I might not need to tell you this,

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:28.920
but here's a Sub InCom for mechanics.

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:31.200
Ensign Bremer...

00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:33.240
Use it if you have to.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:42.290
I'm out of ammo!

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:50.490
It's finally time for my melee fight!

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:56.910
Move!

00:19:57.820 --> 00:19:58.720
You're in my way!

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:00.730
Is that all you've got?

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:13.010
Why is he still on the ground?

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:21.440
Please, Ensign Bremer!

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:24.540
Go back! Go back and save Yuuya... Please!

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:29.190
Again...?

00:20:30.150 --> 00:20:38.510
Do I just have to stand 
there and watch again?

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:46.540
I swore I'd never cry again...

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:48.730
I've endured so many times...

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:58.730
There's no Laser Class observed in this 
area, but I'm dropping altitude anyway.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:05.670
Yuu...

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:06.550
...ya...

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:09.580
Yuuya...

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:11.390
Yuuya!

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:16.740
Yuuya...

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:23.500
I'm not out of it yet!

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:25.890
I won't lose to you!

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:28.970
Damn it!

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:55.820
If I bring it back like this 
even Vincent will be mad at me.

00:22:04.180 --> 00:22:08.000
Damn, I guess the BETA like me.

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:18.070
Thanks for the offer, partner.

00:22:18.890 --> 00:22:22.390
But I made her a promise.

00:22:23.280 --> 00:22:26.400
That I'd take you back.

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:30.130
Let's go, Shiranui!

00:24:07.080 --> 00:24:09.350
A sense of justice and being 
"right" are fine things.

00:24:09.350 --> 00:24:13.680
But if you get in too deep you'll 
lose the people you care about.

00:24:13.680 --> 00:24:15.780
What is the job of an Eishi?

00:24:15.780 --> 00:24:19.300
Your only job is to think 
about that, and then do it.

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:24.270
<b>An Eishi's Honor</b>

00:24:19.860 --> 00:24:22.610
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:22.610 --> 00:24:23.970
An Eishi's Honor
